{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1563432-geist-the-sin-eaters-1st-edition-storyteller\u2019s-screen","id":1563432,"title":"Geist: The Sin-Eaters 1st Edition Storyteller\u2019s Screen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-08-24T14:08:46-07:00","id":1563432,"title":"Geist: The Sin-Eaters 1st Edition Storyteller\u2019s Screen","content":"I\u2019m happy to announce another small contribution to the Storytellers Vault: <b>Geist: The Sin-Eaters Storyteller\u2019s Screen \u2014 First Edition</b>.<br /> <br /> I still have a great deal of affection for the first edition of <i>Geist</i>, and I wanted a practical Storyteller screen that looked and functioned as though it belonged with that edition of the game.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a four-panel screen, with the Storyteller side collecting the rules I thought were most useful to have immediately at hand during play: combat, weapons and armor, extended actions, Psyche and Plasm, Resurrection and the Last Resort, Synergy and discord triggers, Avernian Gates, and ghosts and their powers in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> The player-facing side uses official Storytellers Vault artwork and was designed to sit visually alongside the original First Edition books.<br /> <br /> The PDF contains both sides of the four-panel screen and is available on Storytellers Vault:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/580640/geist-the-sin-eaters-storyteller-s-screen-first-edition?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\">Geist: The Sin-Eaters Storyteller\u2019s Screen \u2014 First Edition</a><br /> <br /> If anyone here is still running or playing First Edition <i>Geist</i>, I\u2019d be particularly interested to know what you find yourself looking up most often during a session. That would be useful for any future revision